 ('servitors','Servitor','Lexicanum contributors','https://wh40k.lexicanum.com/wiki/Servitor','Human-derived flesh/machine workers are tolerated in place of true AI, with variable surviving consciousness and compulsory labor.','Bounded overview/consciousness sections; servitors are not assumed to have all lost personhood, and broad Imperial worlds retain different institutions.'),
 ('mechanicus','Adeptus Mechanicus labor organization','Warhammer 40k Wiki contributors','https://warhammer40k.fandom.com/wiki/Adeptus_Mechanicus','Tech-priests command vast servitor labor forces in forge-world production.','Only labor-role passages; this subset does not establish a separate access system from the retained Imperial servitor/AI-restriction order.'),
 ('titan','Titanian Commonwealth 1e','Eclipse Phase text reproduced by Chuck’s Eclipse Phase Wiki','https://eclipse-phase.fandom.com/wiki/Titanian_Commonwealth_1e','Basic needs, social-money microcorps and direct citizen control of common resources coexist with a contribution contract.','First-edition reproduction, including in-universe viewpoints; second-edition material was located but not merged into this scope.'),
 ('anarchists','Anarchists 1e','Eclipse Phase text reproduced by Chuck’s Eclipse Phase Wiki','https://eclipse-phase.fandom.com/wiki/Anarchists_1e','Shared cornucopia access, collective property, direct democracy and robot delegation coexist with useful human collectives.','Local variations are explicit; not every Autonomist Alliance member is an anarchist commune.'),
 ('economy','The Economy 1e','Eclipse Phase text reproduced by Chuck’s Eclipse Phase Wiki','https://eclipse-phase.fandom.com/wiki/The_Economy_1e','Old, transitional and new economies differ in fabrication access, payment, public basics, taxes, contribution criteria and scarcity.','Bounded economic sections, not the whole rulebook. New-economy participation conditions and scarce living space/morphs must not be erased.'),
 ('economy-primary','Eclipse Phase core economic allowance passage','Posthuman Studios first-edition core text','https://legacy.eclipsephase.com/downloads/Mobile_EclipsePhase_2ndPrinting1.pdf','A short indexed passage states citizenship/contribution conditions and resource quotas for new-economy fabrication.','Indexed text only; no full PDF download, render or complete book read. Allowances are not unlimited.'),
 ('jovian','Jovian Republic 1e','Eclipse Phase text reproduced by Chuck’s Eclipse Phase Wiki','https://eclipse-phase.fandom.com/wiki/Jovian_Republic_1e','The junta restricts public nanofabrication and transhuman technologies while retaining an old-economy hierarchy.','Restrictions coexist with actual elite-controlled fabrication; political suppression is not automatically a separate employment-preservation record.'),
